      "body": "## Summary\n- Add a concise production hardening checklist for the OpenAI-compatible HTTP server.\n- Emphasize reverse proxy / gateway allowlisting, feature flag review, trusted artifact handling, and sensitive logging policy.\n- Keep the wording aligned with existing vLLM security guidance and avoid introducing new vulnerability claims.\n\n## Why\nThe existing security guide already documents the important assumptions: API key auth is not a full server boundary, several operational endpoints should not be exposed, dynamic LoRA loading requires trusted access, tool servers need isolation, and model/cache artifacts are trusted inputs.\n\nThis PR turns those scattered points into an operator-facing checklist so production users have a single place to review before exposing vLLM behind an API or gateway.\n\n## Test plan\n- Docs-only change.\n- Verified the checklist references existing public security guidance.\n",
